# Functional Requirements

Functional requirements define the features and actions that the Help Desk system must provide to its users.

### FR01 — User Registration

The system must allow users to register and create accounts to access the platform.

### FR02 — Authentication

The system must allow users to securely log in and log out.

### FR03 — Ticket Management

The system must allow users to create, view, edit, and track support tickets.

### FR04 — Ticket Status

The system must allow users to change the status of a ticket according to its progress.

### FR05 — Ticket Priority

The system must allow different priority levels to be assigned to tickets.

### FR06 — Categories

The system must allow tickets to be categorized to improve organization and management.

### FR07 — History

The system must maintain a history of changes and actions performed on tickets.

### FR08 — Customer Management

The system must allow users to register and manage customers associated with tickets.

### FR09 — Search and Filters

The system must allow users to search and filter tickets based on different criteria.

### FR10 — Dashboard

The system must provide a dashboard displaying information and indicators related to tickets.

### FR11 — Access Control

The system must allow different access levels to be defined according to user roles.

### FR12 — System Settings

The system must allow the configuration of information required for the system to operate according to the company's environment.
